{
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical pronunciations for names the corpus uses and a plain TTS reader gets wrong.",
    "",
    "Source of truth for voice/lexicon.pls, which is what ElevenLabs actually consumes.",
    "Regenerate the PLS with `python tools/build_lexicon.py` after editing this file.",
    "",
    "Only names that are ACTUALLY mispronounced belong here. Stormwind, Westfall and",
    "Ashenvale are ordinary English compounds and a phoneme rule for them can only make",
    "things worse - every entry is a chance to be wrong, so an entry has to earn its place.",
    "",
    "confidence:",
    "  high  - Blizzard's own voice acting or an unambiguous convention says this.",
    "  check - plausible but unverified, or the community disagrees. Listen before shipping.",
    "",
    "An entry gives EITHER an ipa or an alias, never both:",
    "  ipa    exact, but honoured only by eleven_v3 and eleven_flash_v2. Every other model",
    "         silently ignores it and speaks the default pronunciation.",
    "  alias  a respelling the model reads instead - 'nomeregan', not 'NOME-reh-gan'. Only",
    "         as good as the guess at the new spelling, but honoured by every model.",
    "",
    "The `say` field is the stress-capitals form, for people reading this file. It is never",
    "sent to ElevenLabs - an alias is, and sending stress capitals would have a model read",
    "them as an acronym."
  ],
